dren":[{"type":"text","value":"ctx"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/CapabilityContext.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CapabilityContext"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tname","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TName"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TName"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"},{"type":"text","value":" = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string"}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-declaration","text":"Type Declaration","level":2},{"id":"capabilityname","text":"capabilityName","level":3},{"id":"has","text":"has","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":4},{"id":"ctx","text":"ctx","level":5},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tname","text":"TName","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype Capability<TValue, TName> = readonly [CapabilityGetter<TValue>, CapabilityProvider<TValue>] & object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/capabilities.ts:36](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/capabilities.ts#L36)\n\nA capability handle. It is BOTH a `[get, provide]` tuple (array-destructurable)\nAND the identity used in middleware `requires`/`provides` declarations.\n\nRuntime identity is this object's reference. The `capabilityName` literal is\nused for diagnostics and COMPILE-TIME tracking only — capability names MUST be\nunique across an app or the type-level coverage check conflates them.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### capabilityName\n\n```ts\nreadonly capabilityName: TName;\n```\n\n### has\n\n```ts\nhas: (ctx) => boolean;\n```\n\n**`Internal`**\n\nPresence check for the post-setup assertion.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### ctx\n\n[`CapabilityContext`](../interfaces/CapabilityContext.md)\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue` = `unknown`\n\n### TName\n\n`TName` *extends* `string` = `string`\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: Capability\ntitle: Capability\n---\n\n```ts\ntype Capability<TValue, TName> = readonly [CapabilityGetter<TValue>, CapabilityProvider<TValue>] & object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/capabilities.ts:36](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/activities/chat/middleware/capabilities.ts#L36)\n\nA capability handle. It is BOTH a `[get, provide]` tuple (array-destructurable)\nAND the identity used in middleware `requires`/`provides` declarations.\n\nRuntime identity is this object's reference. The `capabilityName` literal is\nused for diagnostics and COMPILE-TIME tracking only — capability names MUST be\nunique across an app or the type-level coverage check conflates them.\n\n## Type Declaration\n\n### capabilityName\n\n```ts\nreadonly capabilityName: TName;\n```\n\n### has\n\n```ts\nhas: (ctx) => boolean;\n```\n\n**`Internal`**\n\nPresence check for the post-setup assertion.\n\n#### Parameters\n\n##### ctx\n\n[`CapabilityContext`](../interfaces/CapabilityContext.md)\n\n#### Returns\n\n`boolean`\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue` = `unknown`\n\n### TName\n\n`TName` *extends* `string` = `string`\n"}
